.TH SPROUT 1 "October 2026" "sprout v0.3.0-wip" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sprout \- a stupid simple debugger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sprout
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B SPROUT
keeps it stupid simple. it takes no configuration files and requires no arguments.
you cannot invoke it the wrong way, unless you mistype the command.
.PP
.RS
.I note:
sprout can take a \fB\-v\fR flag to be extra verbose, which may help newer developers see basics like OS family.
.RE
.SH BRANDING, PACKAGING, PHILOSOPHY
.TP
.B Branding
SPROUT's official stance on branding is "do whatever you want". the name has
no official casing, and there is no official logo.
.TP
.B Packaging
follow existing conventions, with some leniency in certain areas, such as the
major.minor.patch-tag version scheme introduced by cargo, which is dropped on
most official packaging attempts.
.TP
.B Philosophy
stay simple, never connect to any peer (central server or direct
peer-to-peer), and avoid fetching information that might be deemed sensitive
(username, hostname, IP, ...).
.SH WHAT NOT TO INCLUDE IN A PR
.TP
.B We are not UNIX porn.
SPROUT is not just another UNIX porn fetch utility, you should avoid comparing
it to tools like fastfetch, neofetch, macchina or otherwise.
.TP
.B Functionality >> Presentation
SPROUT should ALWAYS be simple to use, and should not try to be beautiful, it is
not intended to be the pretty thing in the corner that doesn't improve productivity
in any way, instead, it is intended to help you attach relevant information to PRs or
issues, to help make bugs easier to reproduce or diagnose.
.TP
.B Documentation "fixes"
SPROUT documentation is in all lowercase, while you may think that is a mistake, it
is not. it is intended to look less "corporate" or "professional" than other projects.
please do not open PRs or issues attempting to "fix" casing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sprout-modules (7)
